$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Synthetic Procedure I: Amide coupling
reaction for the synthesis of carboxamides 26a-b, 32, 33. To a round
bottom flask was added carboxylic acid (1 equiv) and EDCI (1.05 equiv).
DCM was added and reaction mixture was cooled down to 0 °C and stirred
for 30 min. To this solution was then added respective amine or
piperidium salt (1-2 equiv) with/without DIEA (2 equiv). The reaction
mixture was warmed up to rt and stirred overnight before washing 1x with
5% citric acid, 1x saturated NaHCO3, 1x with H2O and 1x with brine. The
washed organic mixture was then dried with Na2SO4, and concentrated in
vacuo to give a crude residue which was purified using column
chromatography (SiO2, eluent: DCM/MeOH) to afford desired carboxamide.
tert-butyl
((5-(4-benzylpiperazine-1-carbonyl)-4-(4-methoxybenzyl)-4H-thieno[3,2-b]pyrrol-6-yl)methyl)(1-phenylethyl)carbamate
(32) Carboxamide 32 was prepared following the general procedure I using
carboxylic acid 31 (91 mg, 0.18 mmol), 1-benzylpiperazine (37 μL, 0.21
mmol) and EDCI (35 mg, 0.18 mmol). After chromatography (SiO2, eluent:
97.5% DCM, 2.5% MeOH). tert-butyl
4-((3-bromobenzyl)carbamoyl)piperidine-1-carboxylate (10c). Carboxamide
10c was prepared following the general procedure A using carboxylic acid
9 (600 mg, 2.61 mmol), 3-bromobenzylamine (396 μL, 3.14 mmol) and EDCI
(527 mg, 2.75 mmol). After column chromatography (SiO2, eluent: 98% DCM,
2% MeOH). The pure carboxamide 10c was obtained in 71% yield (729 mg).
White Solid. 1H NMR (400MHz; CDCl3) δ 1.44 (s, 9H), 1.55-1.70 (m, 2H),
1.70-1.85 (m, 2H), 2.28 (m, 1H), 2.52-2.90 (m, 2H), 3.95-4.22 (m, 2H),
4.36 (d, J = 5.7 Hz, 2H), 6.49 (m, 1H), 7.05-7.23 (m, 2H), 7.26-7.46 (m,
2H); 13C NMR (100MHz, CDCl3) δ 28.3, 28.5, 42.6, 43.0, 79.6, 122.6,
126.1, 130.1, 130.4, 140.7, 154.6, 174.4; ESI-MS (m/z) calcd for
C18H25BrN2O3 [M+H]+ 397.1; found 397.3.
